          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Lantana involucrata, commonly known as buttonsage, is a species of flowering plant in the verbena family. It is native to the Neotropical realm, where it is widespread in well-drained areas."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Etymology\nThe name Lantana derives from the Latin name of the wayfaring tree Viburnum lantana, the flowers of which superficially resemble Lantana."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "Description\nThe plant blooms and fruits all year long."
          }
        ]
